-# @deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-browser-target
-
-English | [中文](README.zh.md)
-
-Opt-in browser plugin that renders the Chrome extension's Browser Target picker in the Harness composer tool row and its upward `conversation.input.overlay` panel. It starts only when the loopback iframe URL contains `dshBrowserTargetBridge=1`, its per-frame nonce, and the exact Chrome extension parent origin. The extension supplies visible tab metadata and the persisted target policy; the iframe can request only refresh, mode selection, pinned-tab selection, primary-target selection, and a nonce-bound Harness reconnect. Both directions require `window.parent`, the exact origin, and matching nonce; Browser Target state commands additionally require strictly increasing sequence.
-
-Saving the policy never reloads the iframe or reconnects Harness. The control never reads page content, transfers a Browser Target, changes an in-flight Run binding, or contributes model context.
-
-The extension-only adapter also occupies `sidebar.compact.action` with an 18px reconnect icon. The sidebar owns its position between New Session and compact Settings; ordinary web sessions do not register this action.
-
-## Model Experience
-
-None. This package has no tool, session event, prompt section, or model-visible input.
-
-#### KV Cache effect
-
-None.
-
-## Known Limitations and Deferred Work
-
-- The picker is available only inside the Chrome-extension loopback iframe; ordinary web use remains unchanged.
